id: pm-lvd647
title: "GH-666/GH-667: nightly Node 22 stderr and Windows permission-contract regressions"
description: Restore the supported nightly matrix by keeping optional SQLite diagnostics out of machine-readable stderr on Node 22 and making unwritable-memory/history tests assert capability outcomes rather than POSIX-only permission behavior on Windows.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:ci","area:sdk",cross-platform,gh-issue,nightly,node22,windows
created_at: "2026-07-24T12:39:52.841Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T17:19:36.426Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-24T14:16:44.536Z"
author: codex-root-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Optional SQLite capability loading does not leak runtime experimental warnings into CLI/MCP machine channels; tests use scoped deterministic failure seams instead of global warning suppression or POSIX chmod assumptions; Node 22 and Windows focused regressions pass; no nightly job, assertion, or supported runtime is removed; GitHub issues #666 and #667 are linked and closed only after exact hosted proof."
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
release: v2026.7.25
reporter: codex-root-agent
severity: high
repro_steps: "Inspect scheduled run 30072359707 at db1b7111: Node 22 fails three built-CLI/MCP tests because node:sqlite ExperimentalWarning pollutes stderr; Windows fails workspace-memory and drift-scan permission simulations because chmod does not make paths unreadable."
resolution: "Optional node:sqlite loading is gated away from Node 22 machine channels; Windows failure tests use deterministic capability seams; Git workspace containment and results canonicalize 8.3/long paths by filesystem identity."
expected_result: Supported Node and OS matrix tests observe clean machine-readable process channels and deterministic injected filesystem failure semantics; nightly validation passes without silencing unrelated warnings or skipping platform coverage.
actual_result: "PR run 30099757539 passed Node 22 smoke job 89503618661 and Windows regression rerun job 89503591212 (903 tests), with aggregate 100% coverage and all static/typecheck/compat/smoke gates green at ebf0443e."
component: cross-runtime SDK and nightly validation
regression: true
customer_impact: "Daily validation reports red after otherwise-correct SDK changes, obscuring real release risk and making structured CLI/MCP channels unreliable on Node 22."
